+ASUS_EULA_Title=End User License Agreement
+ASUS_EULA_Title_B=End User License Agreement (“EULA”)
+ASUS_EULA_Desc=This End User License Agreement (“EULA”) constitutes a valid and binding agreement between ASUSTeK Computer Inc., on behalf of itself and its affiliates (collectively “ASUS“), and you, as a user, for the use of networking products produced, manufactured, or sold by ASUS (“Products”) and the ASUS Software (“Software”) defined as set forth below. Unless otherwise expressly agreed with ASUS, you acknowledge and agree that the terms of this EULA constitute a part of any form of contract with you. By start using the Products, or by installing and continuing to use the Software, YOU EXPRESSLY ACKNOWLEDGE THAT YOU HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND AND AGREE TO BE BOUND BY THE TERMS OF THIS EULA AND ANY NEW VERSIONS HEREOF. You represent that you are lawfully able to enter into this EULA. When you use the Software or Products, you shall be an adult by the laws of the country where you reside in.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1=Software License
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_1=License
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_1_1=Subject to the terms of this EULA, ASUS hereby grants you a limited, personal, non-commercial, non-exclusive license to use the Software solely as embedded in the Products or for use of the Products. This license shall not be sublicensed, and is not transferable except to a person or entity to whom you transfer ownership of the complete Products containing the Software, or you transfer the ownership of the Products which the Software is used with, and provided you permanently transfer all rights under this EULA and do not retain any full or partial copies of the Software, and the recipient agrees to the terms of this EULA.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_1_2=You acknowledge that ASUS does not provide you with a permanent license to the Software, and agree that ASUS reserves the right to terminate the license to the Software at any time without liability if: (i) you fail to comply with any term of this EULA; or (ii) ASUS decides not to provide the Software in a specific country/region, or ASUS unilaterally decides that it is no longer possible to continue to provide the Software based on commercial considerations.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_2=Software
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_2_1=<b>Software</b> means the software or firmware provided by ASUS in or with the applicable Products, or for use with the Products including but not limited to any future programming fixes, updates, upgrades and modified versions.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_2_2=The Software may be accompanied by other ASUS or third party created software that is licensed under one or more of the Free Open Source Software licenses as listed under www.opensource.org/licenses. Such Free Open Source Software (“FOSS”) is provided to you solely under the terms of the respective license agreement or copyright notice accompanying it or in the FOSS licenses file accompanying the Software. The terms of this EULA do NOT apply to such Free Open Source Software.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_3=Restriction
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_3_1=You shall not modify, compile, reverse engineer, decompile decrypt or disassemble the Software or permit or induce the foregoing except to the extent directly applicable law prohibits enforcement of the foregoing.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_3_2=You acknowledge and agree that if you fail to comply with the restrictions in this Section1.3, ASUS reserves the right to terminate the license to the Software at any time and terminate all or part of the functions of the Product.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_3_3=If the terms of the license agreement or copyright notice of respective FOSS contained in the Software stipulate that you could modify, compile, reverse engineer, decompile decrypt or disassemble the Software, then you could do so in accordance with the terms of such FOSS. However, once the Software is modified and compiled by you, ASUS will not bear any responsibility to you for such Software and Products which such Software embedded with (including but not limited to warranty liability).
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_4=THE UPDATE Of The SOFTWARE
+ASUS_EULA_Law_1_4_Desc=You understand and agree that in order to ensure the safety of the Products and ensure compliance with law/regulations, ASUS reserves the right to mandatary update the Software at any time without your consent, so as to solve material security issues or meet legal/ regulatory requirements.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2=The Usage Of The Products
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_1=Product Description
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_1_1=The functions of the Products may vary slightly depending on the region where such Products are sold. You should check the specifications and functions of the Products by yourself when purchasing such Products.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_1_2=The warranty of the Products is subject to the applicable warranty card and warranty terms with such Products. You acknowledge and agree that ASUS only provides limited paid maintenance services for the Products after the expiration of the warranty period, and the conditions of the relevant paid maintenance services will be implemented in accordance with ASUS regulations.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_2=Restrictions
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_2_1=You shall use the Products in accordance with the relevant user manuals and instructions for the Products, and shall comply with all the terms of this EULA and not use the Products for illegal or improper purposes. If ASUS finds that you fail to comply with the terms of this EULA or use the Products illegally or improperly, ASUS reserves the right to terminate all or part of the functions of the Product. You are solely responsible for your illegal or improper use of the Products.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_2_2_2=You acknowledge and agree that ASUS has the right, without any liability, to temporarily or permanently suspend, modify or terminate the application, service and/or any of its functions at any time based on commercial considerations without notice to you.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_3=Third-Party Products And Services
+ASUS_EULA_Law_3_Desc=You may be able to use or obtain products or services provided by third-party when you are using the Products. You acknowledge and agree that these products and services are provided by third-party and have nothing to do with ASUS. No express or implied warranties are given by ASUS for the products or services provided by any third-party. You shall bear all of the relevant risks by yourself when using third-parties' products or services. ASUS is not responsible for the products, services or/and offers provided by any third-party. If you have any claims or requests for the products, services or/and offers, you should and agree to contact such third-party and negotiate with them by yourself.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_4=Rights To Amend
+ASUS_EULA_Law_4_Desc=You acknowledge and agree that ASUS reserves the right to modify the terms of this EULA at any time. ASUS will announce such modifications on the ASUS Software/web GUI interface. If you continue to use the Software and/or the Products after any modification is announced, it shall mean that you have accepted such modifications and agree to be bound by the modified terms.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_5=Confidentiality
+ASUS_EULA_Law_5_Desc=You shall have a duty to protect and not to disclose or cause to be disclosed in whole or in part of confidential information of the Software and the Products including but not limited to trade secrets, copyrighted material and intellectual property rights in any form to any third party.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_6=Intellectual Property Rights (“IP Rights”)
+ASUS_EULA_Law_6_1=You acknowledge and agree that all IP Rights, title, and interest to or arising from the Software and the Products are and shall remain the exclusive property of ASUS or its licensor. Nothing in this EULA intends to transfer any such IP Rights to you. Any unauthorized use of the IP Rights is a violation of this EULA as well as a violation of intellectual property laws, including but not limited to copyright laws and trademark laws.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_6_2=By sending any information, material, ideas, concepts or techniques except for personal information to ASUS through the Software (“Feedbacks”), you acknowledge and agree that: (i) Your Feedbacks shall not contain confidential or proprietary information; (ii) ASUS is under no obligation of any kind of confidentiality, express or implied, regarding the Feedbacks; (iii) ASUS shall be entitled to use or disclose, at ASUS’s sole discretion, the Feedbacks for any purpose, in any way, worldwide; (iv) Your Feedbacks shall become the property of ASUS without any obligation of ASUS to you; and (v) You are not entitled to any compensation or reimbursement of any kind from.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_7=Term And Termination
+ASUS_EULA_Law_7_Desc=This EULA will be effective as of the date you starting using the Products, or install the Software. You may terminate this License at any time by ceasing all use of the Products and the Software and removing the Software from the Product. Your right will terminate without prior notice from ASUS if we think you fail to comply with any provision of this EULA.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8=Warranty Disclaimer And Limitation Of Liability
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_1=Liability Toward The Software
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_1_1=YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS.” THE ENTIRE RISK AS TO THE QUALITY AND PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE IS WITH YOU, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO RELATED COST OF ALL NECESSARY SERVICING AND REPAIR. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, ASUS MAKES NO WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, WITH RESPECT TO THIS SOFTWARE OR ANY OTHER INFORMATION OR DOCUMENTATION PROVIDED UNDER THIS EULA OR FOR THIS SOFTWARE, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO ANY WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY OR FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE OR AGAINST INFRINGEMENT, OR ANY WARRANTY ARISING OUT OF USAGE OR OUT OF COURSE OF PERFORMANCE. ASUS ALSO MAKES NO WARRANTY AS TO THE RESULTS THAT MAY BE OBTAINED FROM THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE OR AS TO THE ACCURACY OR RELIABILITY OF ANY INFORMATION OBTAINED THROUGH THIS SOFTWARE. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OF CERTAIN WARRANTIES OR THE LIMITATION OR EXCLUSION OF LIABILITY FOR CERTAIN DAMAGES. ACCORDINGLY, SOME OF THE ABOVE DISCLAIMERS AND LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_1_2=IN NO EVENT SHALL ASUS, ITS LICENSORS OR ANY OF THEIR RESPECTIVE OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AGENTS OR AFFILIATES BE LIABLE FOR ANY CONSEQUENTIAL, INCIDENTAL, DIRECT, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, PUNITIVE, OR OTHER DAMAGES WHATSOEVER (INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, DAMAGES FOR LOSS OF PROFITS, INTERRUPTION, LOSS OF INFORMATION OR DATA, OR OTHER PECUNIARY LOSS) ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS EULA OR THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE OR ANY PART THEREOF, EVEN IF ASUS HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OF CERTAIN WARRANTIES OR THE LIMITATION OR EXCLUSION OF LIABILITY FOR CERTAIN DAMAGES. ACCORDINGLY, SOME OF THE ABOVE DISCLAIMERS AND LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_2=Liability Toward The Products
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_2_Desc=IN NO EVENT SHALL ASUS, ITS LICENSORS OR ANY OF THEIR RESPECTIVE OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AGENTS OR AFFILIATES BE LIABLE FOR ANY CONSEQUENTIAL, INCIDENTAL, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, PUNITIVE (INCLUDING, WITHOUT LIMITATION, DAMAGES FOR LOSS OF PROFITS, INTERRUPTION, LOSS OF INFORMATION OR DATA, OR OTHER PECUNIARY LOSS) ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE PRODUCTS OR ANY PART THEREOF, EVEN IF ASUS HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_8_3=Subject to Section 8.1 and 8.2, and to the extent permitted by relevant laws and regulations, the maximum aggregate liability of ASUS for damages to you arising out of any agreement or order between ASUS and you will not exceed US$100. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OF CERTAIN WARRANTIES OR THE LIMITATION OR EXCLUSION OF LIABILITY FOR CERTAIN DAMAGES. ACCORDINGLY, SOME OF THE ABOVE DISCLAIMERS AND LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_9=Indemnity
+ASUS_EULA_Law_9_Desc=You agree to defend, indemnify and hold harmless ASUS and its affiliates, service providers, syndicators, distributors, licensors, officers, directors and employees, from and against any and all losses, damages, liabilities, and expenses arising out of any claim or demand (including reasonable attorneys' fees and court costs), due to or in connection with your violation of this EULA or any applicable law or regulation, or third-party right.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_10=Severability
+ASUS_EULA_Law_10_Desc=If any terms of this EULA shall be held by a court of competent jurisdiction to be illegal, invalid or unenforceable, the remaining terms shall remain in full force and effect, and the illegal, invalid or unenforceable part will be deemed to be excluded from this EULA and replaced by new terms that are permitted by law and reflect the true intentions of both parties in that part.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_11=No Implied Waivers
+ASUS_EULA_Law_11_Desc=Neither the failure nor any delay by the ASUS in exercising or enforcing any right, power or remedy under this EULA shall operate as a waiver thereof, nor shall any single or partial exercise or enforcement of any such right, power or remedy preclude any other or further exercise or enforcement thereof or the exercise or enforcement of any other right, power or remedy.
+ASUS_EULA_Law_12=Governing Law And Jurisdiction
+ASUS_EULA_Law_12_Desc=All quotations, confirmation of orders, this EULA and sales relationship between you and ASUS shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the location of ASUS, without regard to its conflicts of laws principles. All disputes, controversies or differences which may arise between the parties hereto, out of, in relation to or in connection with this EULA shall be settled through friendly consultations between the parties. If the dispute, controversy or difference cannot be settled, both parties agree to submit to the jurisdiction of the court where the ASUS is located.
+ASUS_EULA_Info=By using ASUS networking products, you agree to be bound by the terms and conditions outlined in the End User License Agreement.
+ASUS_POLICY_Age_Check=I am above the age of 16 years.
+ASUS_POLICY_QIS_Desc=It is important to read this term before utilizing a networking product. By clicking at “Agree” button, you agree to be bound by the terms. ​
+ASUS_POLICY_Update_Notice=Dear users, thank you for your ongoing support of this product. In order to comply with privacy regulations in various countries and further protect your data, we have updated the ASUS Privacy Notice. Please update it before using ASUS networking products.
+ASUS_POLICY_Read_Again=Read again
+ASUS_POLICY_Know_Risk=I understood the risk
+ASUS_POLICY_Notice_1=Please be advised that disagreeing with ASUS PRIVACY NOTICE may result in the inability to update to the latest firmware version and unable to receive the most up-to-date protection on your ASUS networking products;  However, to protect the security of your router and ensure the compliance with laws, for upgrades addressing important security issues or meeting legal/regulatory requirements , those upgrades will still be downloaded and installed automatically.
+ASUS_POLICY_Notice_2=Declining certain information may limit the functionality of the following features that rely on that information.
+ASUS_POLICY_Scroll_Down=Please scroll to the bottom
+ASUS_POLICY_Function_Confirm=To use this function, please agree the ASUS PRIVACY NOTICE.
+Reading=Read
+ASUS_PP_Info=We appreciate your interest in ensuring the privacy and security of your information while using ASUS networking products. We would like to invite you to read and familiarize yourself with the ASUS Privacy Notice, which outlines the measures we take to collect, handle, and protect your personal information.​
+ASUS_PP_Title=ASUS PRIVACY NOTICE
+ASUS_PP_Desc=Welcome to use this ASUS Software/web GUI interface (“this Software”/ “this Interface”) for ASUS networking products (“ASUS Product”)! Please read this Notice carefully:
+ASUS_PP_Law_1=In order to provide you with the following functions, <b><u>by clicking “Agree” below, you agree to share your following data related to your ASUS Product(s) associated with this Software/ Interface:</u></b>
+ASUS_PP_Law_1_1=Function of account log-in: For easier management of your ASUS Product(s) and related services (such as binding your ASUS Product(s) under your account), you may need to provide ASUS with your login email address of this Software.
+ASUS_PP_Law_1_2=Functions of ASUS firmware and security upgrades, DDNS (Dynamic Domain Name System for connecting ASUS Product(s) with changing or fixed IP address), remote access service that allows this Software and some third party services (Alexa/Google Assistant/IFTTT) to remotely connect to your ASUS Product(s), backup/transfer service for the configuration settings among ASUS Products, management of multiple ASUS Products and push notification service:
+ASUS_PP_Law_1_3=In order to provide you with the above functions and to assess and improve ASUS services and improve stability, you may need to provide ASUS with your IP address, MAC address, DDNS name, the country of manufacture, model name, firmware and software module version, security version, manufacture date and version of hardware, firmware update data (such as execution method, time and numbers of firmware update), system status (such as usage status of fan, CPU, RAM, flash memory and voltage), numbers and time of boot-ups, the time/network/LAN-port you use to connect to your ASUS Product(s), crash history, product name and code, the number of times of security events with ASUS, login/usage status, as well as screen size, language settings and type of mobile device (such as iOS device).
+ASUS_PP_Law_2=Third party-related services:
+ASUS_PP_Law_2_1=Alexa/Google Assistant/IFTTT: If you use any of these services, you agree that ASUS may share your IP address and Mac address to Amazon.com Inc./Google Inc./ IFTTT Inc. in order to remotely connect your ASUS Product(s) with these services.
+ASUS_PP_Law_2_2=Third party Software Development Kit (SDK) for push notification function: To provide you with the above service, you agree that ASUS may use SDKs developed by third parties. We may change the list of SDKs from time to time, and update the list via this Notice. Below is the current SDK for this function: Google Firebase for Android SDK, with its data collection notice released by Google Inc. at <a href="https://firebase.google.com/docs/android/play-data-disclosure" target="_blank">https://firebase.google.com/docs/android/play-data-disclosure</a>.
+ASUS_PP_Law_2_3=For the services provided by third parties, please note that your information may be collected by those third parties. For more information, please refer to the privacy- related statement issued by the third parties.
+ASUS_PP_Law_3=Please kindly note: If you click “Disagree” below or disable the sharing of the above data of paragraph 1 with ASUS through “Administration” page of this Interface, or if you are a child thus preventing the collection of the above data by ASUS, it may result in the following effects:
+ASUS_PP_Law_3_1=The inability to update to the latest firmware version and unable to receive the most up-to-date security protection on your ASUS Product(s). However, to protect the security of your ASUS Product(s) and ensure the compliance with laws, for upgrades addressing important security issues or meeting legal/regulatory requirements, those upgrades will still be downloaded and installed automatically.
+ASUS_PP_Law_3_2=In this case, ASUS will collect your IP address, hashed MAC address, the country of manufacture, model name, firmware and software module version and security version, which is necessary data for ASUS to deliver these important upgrades to your ASUS Product(s) associated with this Software/ Interface.
+ASUS_PP_Law_3_3=The functions listed in paragraph 1 for this Software/ Interface may not be worked normally without the above data of paragraph 1 for providing those services. The essential functions of ASUS Products will not be affected, such as internet connection and local settings stored in your ASUS Product(s).
+ASUS_PP_Law_4=ASUS is committed to protecting and respecting your privacy; you may visit “Administration->Policy” at this Interface to enable/disable the sharing of your above data with ASUS at all times. To know more about how ASUS protects your privacy, please visit <a href="https://nw-dlcdnet.asus.com/support/forward.html?model=&type=Policy&lang=EN" target="_blank">ASUS’ Privacy Policy</a>.
+ASUS_PP_End=To protect your privacy, please proceed with the age check. If you are a child under the age of <u>16</u>, to protect your privacy, generally we will not collect the above data in paragraph 1 through this Software/ Interface except when providing you with upgrades addressing important security issues or meeting legal/regulatory requirements as mentioned above in paragraph 3(1).
